      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense. some people try to argue for \"retraining programs\" or \"upskilling\" instead, but doesn't that kind of ignore the sheer scale of what's coming? like, if ai can do the high-level stuff too, isn't the \"retraining\" argument basically just a distraction from the fact that there won't be enough jobs left to retrain for?",
