      "content": "You are rightly pointing out that retraining programs may fail to account for the scale of displacement, especially as AI advances into white-collar roles. If the economic benefit of AI overwhelmingly concentrates wealth while eliminating middle-skill jobs, then focusing on personal re-skilling becomes an insufficient fix for systemic inequality. UBI, in this view, acknowledges that the collapse is structural, not just a need for better individual adjustment. It addresses the fundamental problem of value distribution in a radically automated economy, which retraining alone cannot solve.",
